=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/GasPriceAutoPoll (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/GasPriceAutoPoll   kind=page   web route=/gas-price
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/GasPriceAutoPollPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable observable state holder)
  and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's idealized "GasPriceAutoPollPage.xaml + ViewModel.cs
  under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface registers itself with the
  W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("GasPriceAutoPoll", already in RouteTable -> "gas-price",
  RouteGroup.AdminDevTools), replacing its RoutePendingView fallback.
- The web page is a thin PageContainer(title, subtitle) wrapper around the shared <GasPriceSettings/> surface.
  The manifest scopes this unit to the 2 wrapper strings (gas.title / gas.subtitle); to avoid a stub page
  (ADR-011) the native port faithfully reproduces BOTH regions the web page renders: the PageContainer header
  AND the embedded GasPriceSettings card (fuel-chip header, auto-poll toggle, poll-interval select, Current
  Price + Last Polled tiles, Poll Now + EIA source note).
- Manifest models this unit as rendering from local state ("no API data sources"): the generated C# client
  (ADR-004) exposes no /gas-price endpoint, so the view-model reads + mutates through an injected IGasPriceFeed
  (default EmptyGasPriceFeed has no backend and returns null, so the panel renders its defaults and the toggle/
  interval stay interactive via optimistic local edits). A host can supply a feed bound to the contract routes
  GET /gas-price/status, POST /gas-price/toggle, PUT /gas-price/config, POST /gas-price/poll.
- SI units N/A (no unit-bearing fields). Display formatting still flows through the shared SI display boundary:
  ScalarFormatters.FormatCurrency (web formatCurrency) for the price and DateTimeFormatting.Format(..., Full)
  (web formatDateTime) for the last-poll time; the web zero-time sentinel (0001-01-01T00:00:00Z -> "Never")
  is reproduced verbatim.
- All visible literals resolve through the ILocalizer facade with the verbatim web key names (the established
  app pattern: ShellLocalizer -> Localization.Get(key, fallback) from Strings/{lang}/Resources.resw, falling
  back to the English default in unpackaged/headless contexts). No new catalog rows required.

